          "answer_excerpt": "# Technical Analysis of Plant Condition Monitoring Records (Records 0000000\u20130000017)\n\n## 1. Scope and Method\n\nThis report analyzes 18 condition-monitoring records spanning five asset classes (turbines, valves, compressors, separators, heat exchangers, plus one reactor, scrubber, and pipeline). Each record contains five measured parameters: discharge/suction pressure (kPa), process temperature (\u00b0C), volumetric flow (m\u00b3/h), casing vibration velocity (mm/s RMS), and reported efficiency (%).\n\nBecause the dataset lacks nameplate data, design duty points, and historical baselines, the analysis relies on:\n\n- **Cross-asset comparison** \u2014 identifying statistical outliers within the fleet.\n- **Type-specific expectations** \u2014 e.g., turbines normally run hot with high flow; separators normally run cool; heat exchangers should show a meaningful temperature differential.\n- **ISO 10816/20816 vibration severity zones** \u2014 the standard framework for rotating machinery velocity readings (Zone A/B: acceptable, Zone C: restricted operation, Zone D: danger).\n\nFleet statistics for context:\n\n| Parameter | Min | Max | Approx. Mean |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Pressure (kPa) | 92 |",
